{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact diagnosis head f50bde50478fdf17655557a50e645d29376848f9 on builder/receive-pack-diagnosis-20261102, tree 4be9676e, for request 6ce82b92 under promise 7035c1a1 and review request 98095c3c. This approval covers the record of one reproduction and its replay. It claims no fix, no deployment, no settlement of G3's unknown merge stage and no G3 acceptance.\n\nScope. Main ec48e2d5 is the parent, and the worktree is clean. The one commit adds the note and its manifest, and its message passes. git diff 1ca60fee f50bde50 lists only paths under notes/, so the source, tests and configuration equal O1's gated checkpoint, whose gate.exit reads exit 0. The documentation-only rule in docs/testing.md applies, and no new gate is due.\n\nThe diagnosis holds against the source:\n\n- packages/git/src/http.ts:256 returns unknown unless the reply parses to exactly three records: unpack status, one command status and one flush. A fourth record, a second flush, takes that path before the status check and before read-back.\n- http.ts and packages/scope/src/github-host.ts hash to 18bb115b… and df0c0737… at both afdd8ee5 and ec48e2d5. The probe ran the same parser that main holds, and that the mini serves.\n- The replay record gives the reply's layout: 76 bytes with SHA-256 e9e7e6ef…, an unpack-ok packet at offset 0, the own ref's ok at offset 14, and flushes at offsets 68 and 72. Removing only the last four bytes makes the unchanged code accept. The missing-flush, third-flush and wrong-ref controls stay unknown.\n- A read-only GitHub API read of repository 1442980126 shows the scratch branch at 2f372581 and main unchanged at dee19e0b, as the note says.\n\nThe note keeps the limit in the right place. The original G3 attempt left no wire bytes, so this record shows a concrete cause, not the original one.\n\nEvidence. The manifest hashes to 6681c32c…, as the request states. All 32 public files match their sizes and digests, they are read-only, and the uni